  "id": "Compound::DB00346 - Gene::146",
  "verbalization": "Alfuzosin is linked to Adra1d through a series of molecular and physiological mechanisms that involve the alpha-adrenergic receptor. The evidence suggests that Alfuzosin causes Intraoperative Floppy Iris Syndrome, which is then mediated by Tamsulosin or Silodosin, both of which bind to Adra1d. This indicates a potential pathway where Alfuzosin, through its effects on the body, indirectly influences the activity of Adra1d. The shared characteristic of these drugs as alpha-adrenergic antagonists and their common ancestry as organic cyclic compounds further supports a unified mechanism of action. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Alfuzosin in modulating Adra1d activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
